        "orario": "09:17",
        "timestamp": 1775978264,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Among Magyar's supporters, \"one word keeps coming up: hope\" Europe Issued on: 12/04/2026 - 09:17 \"This is a clear battle between two men, the incumbent, Prime Minister Viktor Orban and far right leader, and the opposition leader Peter Magyar, a conservative, pro-European figure,\" said FRANCE 24 Journalist Clovis Casali, reporting from Budapest, Hungary. Among Magyar's supporters, \"one word keeps coming up: hope\", said Casali. Click on the video for more. 'Trump harbors an unexplained sympathy for Vladimir Putin', Ukrainian analyst says 10/04/2026 Europe Hungary: Is Viktor Orban Russia's 'Trojan horse' in the EU? 10/04/2026 Europe France plans 36 billion euro boost to rearmament, nuclear deterrent expansion 08/04/2026 Europe EU farm fraud scandal rocks Greek government, PM urges swift action 07/04/2026 Europe French nationals leave Iran after more than three years in detention 07/04/2026 Europe European Commissioner Síkela announces 'new approach' for global health 07/04/2026 Health Manlio Graziano: 'Europe still needs the US but they know they cannot trust Americans anymore' 07/04/2026 Europe 'Vladimir Putin absolutely nervous' about Hungary's election, expert says 06/04/2026 Europe Russia says 'highly likely' that Ukraine planted explosives near gas pipeline 06/04/2026 Europe"
